\section{Introduction}
Northern Subanen (ISO 639-3: stb) is an Austronesian language of the Philippines, part of the Subanen dialect cluster in Zamboanga del Norte and neighbouring provinces. The search found nothing specific to Northern Subanen. The results covered the Subanen group in general and the related Western Subanon variety. Nothing below should be taken as a Northern Subanen resource unless it says so.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No Northern Subanen primers, textbooks or school materials were found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia overview of the Subanen languages, which lists Northern Subanen as one subdivision: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subanen_languages}
\item Omniglot page on Western Subanon, a related variety (not Northern). It reports that a dictionary and literacy materials were being produced for that variety: \url{https://omniglot.com/writing/westernsubanon.htm}
\item ``A grammar of Western Subanon'' (De La Salle University repository), about the related Western variety: \url{https://animorepository.dlsu.edu.ph/faculty_research/9373}
